# The Flentrop of 1958, Adolphus Busch Hall: a stop
# for dacvoice (voices/README.md, "Stops"). The division's lines (n,
# frame, envelope, chiff) are the same in each of its stops, so they mix.
name Roerfluit 8
family Hoofdwerk
n 10
frame 8
start 18 dB
attack 0.012 s
peak 0 dB
decay 0 dB/s
sustain 0 dB
release 0.05 s
chiff 0.012 s 16 dB 2 16
# Hoofdwerk: a half-stopped chimney flute at 8 feet. Its harmonics, and its
# level 6 dB under the Valkfluit 2, are measured from the opening of Biggs's
# recording of the Little Fugue, where these two stops sound together.
harmonics 1 1.0  2 0.018  3 0.035  4 0.01  5 0.031  6 0.006  7 0.016
level 6 dB
# The voicing (voices/README.md, "The voicing"): the speech by the pipe's
# size, and Busch Hall, where the organ stands.
rise 10
room busch
# The edge tone, the wind at the mouth of a flute that sounds the converter's
# fundamental.
edge -22
# The celeste: a second read of the table at half the rate, 2 cents
# sharp, a rank a little off the unison.
celeste 2
